OPEN

The lifetime defect D-C7 names is FIXED and was qualified by attempt 1 to within 192 bytes,
three fresh processes, byte-identical: the same test that left 923 776 B per L1 bank
allocated at Milestone B leaves 131 520 B after the fix, so 792 256 B come back against a
GALAXY_GLOBAL_CB_SIZE of 792 064 B (logs/d11_q_two_pools_run{1,2,3}.log, commit d40b2093783).

THE BRIEF'S GATE IS NOT MET. It asks for two full models built, used and closed in one
process with the second creating its global circular buffer, three fresh processes. What
stands in the way has changed twice and is now named:

  D-C13 (attempt 1)  the second model's global CB failed to allocate: 1 261 952 B free but
                     the largest contiguous block 759 488 B, 32 576 B short. Fragmentation,
                     not exhaustion. SUPERSEDED - with commit 32e552bb0b2 the allocation
                     succeeds.
  D-C14 (attempt 3)  the second model's first DECODE hangs, in
                     FDMeshCommandQueue::wait_for_outstanding_reads under
                     ttnn.synchronize_device, with both models' weights resident.
                     Backtrace: tttv2_milestone_c_runs/c-defects3/logs/m1b_hang_bt.txt
                     Run: logs/m1b_qwen_two_pools_r1.log (rc=143 after 21 min).
                     Attempt 2's logs/e1_qwen_two_pools_l1.log hung at the same point under
                     an earlier version of this code, so D-C14 predates the D-C13 fix and
                     was masked by it.

  D-C14's cause, read out of tt_metal: the ttnn program cache belongs to the mesh device,
  outlives a model's close(), and keys on op-and-config hashes - so two structurally
  identical Galaxy models in one process share compiled decode programs, and those programs
  carry the first model's global circular buffer addresses
  (CircularBufferImpl::set_global_circular_buffer captures buffer_address() and
  config_address() once; dispatch.cpp:3035 re-sends the captured pair every launch). The
  buffer must therefore land on the same L1 blocks for every model in the process.

  The fix for that is IMPLEMENTED and HOST-QUALIFIED, not on silicon: GlobalCBPlacement, a
  record the owner accepts by injection, held per mesh device for the life of the process by
  models/common/models/galaxy/prefetch.py. test_prefetcher_2d.py 33 passed, including a case
  that fails without the shared record.

  It could not be qualified because the mesh lost board 23 at 11:10Z:
  "Read 0xffffffff over PCIe ID 23: the board should be reset", and ten reset attempts over
  four mechanisms (-glx_reset x7, -glx_reset_auto, -glx_reset_tray, -r 23) all ended
  "POST_RESET failed for device 23".
  Logs: tttv2_milestone_c_runs/c-defects3/logs/{mesh_state_1120Z,reset_1121Z,reset_1130Z,
  reset_auto_1150Z,reset_tray3_1152Z,reset_r23_1152Z,reset_1156Z}.log

